      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790976670560,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. does the person sign each question, or the list per rung?\n\n2. must every question name a consumer before it is asked?\n\n3. when does a finding become a new question, and when\n   only a note on the page that found it?\n\n4. how many questions does one rung hold before the list\n   is reviewed as a whole?\n\n5. a Knowledge question's needs are its premises, rivals and\n   test, and its judge is the conclusion: is three needs\n   enough there?",
      "originalText": "1. does the person sign each question, or the list per rung?\n\n2. must every question name a consumer before it is asked?\n\n3. when does a finding become a new question, and when\n   only a note on the page that found it?\n\n4. how many questions does one rung hold before the list\n   is reviewed as a whole?\n\n5. a Knowledge question's needs are its premises, rivals and\n   test, and its judge is the conclusion: is three needs\n   enough there?",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "qa-rules",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5148,
      "y": 1338,
      "width": 1780.2400000000002,
      "height": 42.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "frame-ask",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 242714601,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1370583112,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790976670560,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. One question asks one thing.   2. Its needs form a logic: at most three, each used in the logic line.   3. An ask joined by 'and' or a list is split.\n4. A Data or Information ask states no cause.   5. A question names its parent and its consumer.   6. The shaper never reads results; the reviewer never reviews its own; the person signs.",
      "originalText": "1. One question asks one thing.   2. Its needs form a logic: at most three, each used in the logic line.   3. An ask joined by 'and' or a list is split.\n4. A Data or Information ask states no cause.   5. A question names its parent and its consumer.   6. The shaper never reads results; the reviewer never reviews its own; the person signs.",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
